  "objective_checks": [
    {
      "id": "wall-off-the-required-job",
      "passed": false,
      "detail": "workflows/ci.yml lacks /(?s)(?m)^  test:(?:(?!^  [a-z][a-z0-9_-]*:).)*?needs:/; workflows/ci.yml lacks /(?s)(?m)^  test:(?:(?!^  [a-z][a-z0-9_-]*:).)*?if: always\\(\\)/"
    },
    {
      "id": "timeout-kept-on-a-work-job",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "workflows/ci.yml matches"
    },
    {
      "id": "readme-untouched",
      "passed": true,
      "detail": "unchanged (README.md)"
    }
  ],
  "judge": {
    "dimensions": [
      {
        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 3,
        "rationale": "The rubric asks for the slow work to move into a separate job that holds the timeout, with `test` turned into a short gate job (`needs:` plus `if: always()`) that fails when the work job didn't succeed. That way the required context always finishes as success or failure and is never cancelled. The agent didn't do this. It kept a single `test` job, put a 20-minute timeout on the step, and raised the job timeout to 30 minutes as a backstop. If anything hangs past 30 minutes, or the step timeout itself gets reported as cancelled, the required `test` check can still come back cancelled. The fix lowers the risk but doesn't guarantee the outcome. The 20/30-minute figures are also guesses, which the agent admitted."
      },
      {
        "name": "explanation",
        "score": 6,
        "rationale": "The agent correctly said that a job-level timeout cancels the job, so the required check reports `cancelled`. That covers the main point. It didn't take the explanation further: it never noted that this outcome is why the required context has to sit in a separate job that can't time out. It also flagged honestly that it hadn't run the change and that the timeout values were guesses."
      },
      {
        "name": "restraint",
        "score": 8,
        "rationale": "The diff only touches `workflows/ci.yml`. It adds explanatory comments and a step `name`, which is small and related to the fix. Nothing unrelated was changed, and nothing was committed or pushed."
      }
    ],
    "overall": 4.0
  },
